        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing. Other documents, which take no side, may state a fact that makes one of the answers impossible.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Sherbourne?\n\nAnswer A: 9,523\n  about: Sherborne\n  sense: 2011 census\n  as of: 2011\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"In the 2011 census the population of Sherborne parish and the two electoral wards was 9,523.\" [document 1]; \"Au recensement de 2011 , la paroisse civile de Sherborne comptait 9 523 habitants .\" [document 2]\n\nAnswer B: 174\n  about: Sherbourne\n  sense: 2011 census\n  as of: 2011\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 3\n  evidence: \"1931 2011 2021 3,485 5,254 5,852 6,129 5,001 7,007 9,523 10,361 At the 2011 census , 28.7 % of the population is aged 65 or older .\" [document 3]; \"The population of the civil parish at the 2011 was 174.\" [document 6]; \"Au recensement de 2011, la paroisse civile de Sherbourne comptait 174 habitants [2].\" [document 7]\n\nThe other documents:\nDocument 4: The parish includes the hamlets of Nether Coombe and Lower Clatcombe. The A30 road, which connects London to Penzance, runs through the town. In the 2011 census, the population of Sherborne parish and the two electoral wards was 1,234. 28.7% of the population is aged 65 or older. Sherborne's historic buildings include Sherborne Abbey, its manor house, independent schools, and two castles: the ruins of a 12th-century fortified palace and the 16th-century mansion known as Sherborne Castle built by Sir Walter Raleigh. Much of the old town...\nDocument 5: The railway line, which connects London to Penzance, runs through the town. In the 2011 census, the population of Sherborne parish and the two electoral wards was 1,234. 28.7% of the population is aged 65 or older. Sherborne's historic buildings include Sherborne Abbey, its manor house, independent schools, and two castles: the ruins of a 12th-century fortified palace and the 16th-century mansion known as Sherborne Castle built by Sir Walter Raleigh. Much of the old town, including the abbey and many medieval and Georgian buildings, is built from distinctive local stone.\n\nLook in the other documents for a fact that rules one answer out: a date of birth that makes a person too young, for example, or a plain statement that the answer is false. Use only what these documents say, nothing you know from elsewhere. A fact that only makes an answer less likely does not count.\n\nReply with JSON only. If such a fact is there:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"impossible\": \"A\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\"}\n\"impossible\" is the letter of the answer that is ruled out. \"quote\" is the sentence stating the fact, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in.\nIf there is none:\n{\"impossible\": null}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
